{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 30,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was invited here, to Munich, by BMW the sponsor of this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4840,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find out why the future of cars is electric."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8800,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But electric cars are actually nothing new -- they date back to 1832,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well before the first gasoline-powered car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17160,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the first car to go faster than a hundred kilometers per hour"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20960,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was in 1899, an electric one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24080,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called the Jamais Contente, meaning \"never satisfied\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But people were apparently satisfied with electric cars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32640,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 1910, they were almost twice as common on American roads as internal combustion engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38240,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then came the Model T, which at $650 was significantly cheaper than comparable electric cars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as gas stations popped up around the country, they could be quickly refueled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50080,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allowing you to travel farther, faster, and cheaper than electric cars, which took a long time to recharge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by 1935, the electric vehicle had been commercially obliterated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63000,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But electric cars were still useful for some things:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66400,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the vacuum of space, an electric vehicle was the obvious choice for the Apollo lunar roving vehicle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72120,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a single-use vehicle due to its non rechargeable silver zinc potassium hydroxide battery,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79080,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it had a range of just 92 kilometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82560,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the astronauts never needed even half of this range."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87840,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the Munich Olympics in 1972, to lead marathon runners in their race,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BMW created an electric version of its two series car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96760,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The car ran on 12 large car batteries for a maximum range of 60 kilometers, or 37 miles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103840,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This demonstrated the benefits of electric vehicles: they can run quietly with no emissions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109880,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it also illustrated their limitations: with the battery technology available at the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115880,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric cars were expensive and short-range, impractical for everyday use."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122680,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why are electric cars the future?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2020, BMW is launching the IX3 all-electric sport utility vehicle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131280,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they plan to have 25 electrified vehicles in their fleet by 2023."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136200,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of their concept cars, like the Vision M Next, are electric vehicles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140960,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they have a Formula-E car which can now run a whole race on a single battery pack."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is all made possible by developments in battery technology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152040,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Batteries have gotten a lot better,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particularly with the introduction of lithium ion batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157720,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First used in mobile phones about 30 years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lithium ion batteries have almost two times more energy in the same volume"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165200,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the next-best battery chemistry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167560,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of their use in many consumer products like phones and laptops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their manufacturing costs continue to decline,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174320,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "driven by manufacturing and supply chain optimization."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177720,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the last three decades, the energy density has increased both per unit mass and per unit volume,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184760,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while the price has plummeted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186840,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is unlike internal combustion engines which, after a century of development,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191440,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have few areas left for improvement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195240,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the reality is, you don't really travel that far in a car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199200,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The batteries available today are good enough for all but the longest road trips."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203720,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the US, 99% of trips are under 160 kilometers, or 100 miles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And electric cars are just better vehicles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215840,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here are my top 10 reasons why:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First: more torque from a standstill."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2. Thanks to the batteries under the floor, they have a low center of mass and so better handling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227640,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3. Since you can drive electric motors independently,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230720,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can have precise control over each wheel for maximum traction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235800,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4. Electric cars are quieter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5. Electric cars are cheaper to run than gas cars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242680,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because gas is more expensive than electricity for the same distance traveled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247160,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6. Electric cars are more efficient than gas cars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250360,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both in converting stored energy into energy of motion and in regenerating some of that energy when braking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "7. You never have to visit a gas station, because you can recharge at home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264000,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "8. There's less maintenance: fewer moving parts, no oil changes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the brakes wear out less often thanks to regenerative braking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271720,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "9. And depending on the source of electricity, in my case, solar panels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric cars don't produce any CO2 at all, so they don't contribute to climate change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, as cars become essentially computers on wheels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric vehicles are leading the way towards self-driving cars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288000,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alright we're gonna start our ride in an autonomous vehicle, my first time ever:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Level 4 autonomy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once this becomes commonplace, it's likely we'll change how we see cars:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298320,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from something we own that sits idle for most of its existence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302440,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to transportation as a service,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304760,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something we ride in to get from point A to point B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and something we share with others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are still a lot of details to work out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's clear to me that the future of cars is electric, autonomous, and shared."
    } ]
  } ]
}
